dzn: Give color attachments that are input attachments simultaneous access

A subpass can read, as an input attachment, the color attachment it renders
to: a feedback loop, which Vulkan games use for programmable blending.
Destiny Rising's deferred renderer does that in most of its lighting
subpasses, in GENERAL layout. Direct3D 12 defines reading a texture while it
is bound as a render target only for textures created with
D3D12_RESOURCE_FLAG_ALLOW_SIMULTANEOUS_ACCESS, which drivers never compress.
For any other texture the shader can read stale or compressed data: on an
AMD Radeon 780M under WSL2, Destiny Rising's sky came out black.

dzn_image_create gives such images simultaneous access, as it already does
for VK_SHARING_MODE_CONCURRENT ones, except depth/stencil and multisampled
images, which Direct3D 12 does not allow it, and images of external memory:
importing memory for a dedicated image requires every flag of the image on
the exported resource, which another image or a buffer made without it, so
the import failed with VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE (Wuthering Waves,
through Venus, then stopped at its first frame). Dozen keeps
simultaneous-access images in the common layout, also while rendering, so
their barriers stay as they were.

diff --git a/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_image.c b/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_image.c
index 3023adf..a16e0a8 100644
--- a/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_image.c
+++ b/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_image.c
@@ -297,7 +297,19 @@ dzn_image_create(struct dzn_device *device,
       }
    }
 
-   if (pCreateInfo->sharingMode == VK_SHARING_MODE_CONCURRENT &&
+   /* A color attachment that is also an input attachment can be read by a
+    * subpass that renders to it: a feedback loop, which Vulkan games use
+    * for programmable blending. Direct3D 12 defines reading a texture while
+    * it is bound as a render target only for simultaneous-access textures,
+    * which are never compressed; for any other texture the shader can read
+    * stale or compressed data (Destiny Rising's sky came out black on AMD).
+    * Not for an image of external memory: an imported resource must have
+    * every flag of the image, and the exporter's has no such flag.
+    */
+   if ((pCreateInfo->sharingMode == VK_SHARING_MODE_CONCURRENT ||
+        ((usage & VK_IMAGE_USAGE_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_BIT) &&
+         (usage & VK_IMAGE_USAGE_INPUT_ATTACHMENT_BIT) &&
+         !image->vk.external_handle_types)) &&
        image->desc.Dimension != D3D12_RESOURCE_DIMENSION_BUFFER &&
        !(image->desc.Flags & D3D12_RESOURCE_FLAG_ALLOW_DEPTH_STENCIL) &&
        image->desc.SampleDesc.Count == 1)
